package com.lz.solver.material

/**
 * NDS 2024 Supplement, Table 4D: Reference Design Values for Visually Graded Timbers (5" x 5" and larger).
 * Values are in psi, exactly as printed, for normal load duration; dry service unless [Row.wetServiceValues] (see
 * below). Checked by two independent extractions of the PDF (a coordinate-based parse and a text-layout parse) that
 * agree on all 250 rows: species, grade name and all seven values. Size classification, specific gravity and agency
 * come from the merged cells of the printed table and were attributed by matching each label to the rows it spans
 * (each attribution was uniquely determined).
 *
 * Column order is as printed: Fb, Ft, Fv, Fc-perp, Fc, E, Emin. Species names and grade names are kept as printed,
 * including the printed inconsistencies ("No.1" in most species but "No. 1" in Douglas Fir-Larch, Redwood and Southern
 * Pine). Agency attribution:
 *  - Douglas Fir-Larch is printed as two separate row sets, one for PLIB (5 grades per size class) and one for WWPA
 *    (6 grades per size class, with Dense and non-Dense No. 2), so rows are looked up by agency as well.
 *  - Sitka Spruce is printed as two separate row sets (PLIB, WWPA) that differ in the No. 2 E and Emin.
 *  - Where one printed block lists several agencies (for example Hem-Fir "PLIB / WWPA"), the rows carry all of them.
 *
 * "Mixed Southern Pine" and "Southern Pine" carry the printed note "(Wet Service Conditons)" [sic]: their tabulated
 * values are for wet service already, and the Table 4D adjustment page says to use them without further wet service
 * adjustment ([Row.wetServiceValues] = true). Southern Pine also lists three extra grades printed as "Dense Select
 * Structural 86", "... 72" and "... 65".
 *
 * Footnote 3: when species are combined, use the lowest value of each property (a design rule, not data).
 * Footnote 2 (Spruce Pine from Mixed Southern Pine) gives only [sprucePineConversion]; no Spruce Pine rows are
 * generated here, and the printed rounding text for E and Emin is garbled in the source ("E; ... E"), so the
 * rounding rules are not encoded.
 *
 * The Table 4D Adjustment Factors page (size factor CF, flat use Cfu for Beams and Stringers, wet service CM) is NOT
 * part of this data and is applied by the design code.
 *
 * This is source data only: NDS 2024 stays blocked for design (see [NdsCodeData]) until the design-value lookup,
 * the 2024 adjustment-factor pages and the species mapping are connected and verified.
 */
object Nds2024Table4D {

    data class Row(
        val species: String,
        val grade: String,
        /** "Beams and Stringers", "Posts and Timbers" or "5"x5" and Larger" (spacing as printed). */
        val sizeClassification: String,
        val fb: Int,
        val ft: Int,
        val fv: Int,
        val fcPerp: Int,
        val fc: Int,
        val e: Int,
        val eMin: Int,
        val specificGravity: Double,
        val gradingRulesAgencies: List<String>,
        /** True for the species printed with "(Wet Service Conditons)": values are already wet service values. */
        val wetServiceValues: Boolean
    )

    /** Footnote 2 conversion factors (Mixed Southern Pine to Spruce Pine). E and Emin share one factor. */
    data class SprucePineConversion(
        val fb: Double, val ft: Double, val fv: Double, val fcPerp: Double, val fc: Double, val eAndEMin: Double
    )

    val sprucePineConversion = SprucePineConversion(fb = 0.78, ft = 0.78, fv = 0.98, fcPerp = 0.73, fc = 0.78, eAndEMin = 0.82)

